    {
      "id": "suite-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Run the suite",
      "position": {
        "x": -80,
        "y": -480
      },
      "width": 860,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Workspace Boundary Smoke Suite\n\nUse **Clear workspace** before each numbered scenario. Open the named fixtures with these Portal cards or **Open alongside**. Do not save mutations unless you intentionally want to inspect their JSON.\n\n## Bridge checks\n1. Open **Bridge Provider** alone: three export capabilities appear; no cross-graph edge appears.\n2. Add **Matching Consumer**: exactly one amber workspace edge connects `export-matched` to `import-provider`.\n3. Add **Consumer Without Import**: no additional edge appears.\n4. Add **Wrong Import Identity**: no additional edge appears.\n\n## Port and Portal checks\n5. Open **Port Provider** and **Creation Target**. Drag the cyan Task Port handle into Creation Target: one new Portal appears there, targeting the provider's `task-port`.\n6. Drag the same handle into empty workspace: a new graph appears containing one Declaration and one Portal.\n7. Open **Portal Navigation**, note its three authored nodes, then click its Portal: Port Provider opens alongside and Portal Navigation still has three nodes.\n\n## Portal identity dispatch\n8. Open **Identity Dispatch** and click **Same nodeId**: the participant graph must expand into the active semantic node; no new workspace frame appears.\n9. Return to **Identity Dispatch** and click **Different nodeId**: the target graph opens alongside as a separate workspace frame. The suite entry uses ordinary navigation. Inside the fixture, scenario 8 explicitly expands a reciprocal participant with the same declaration `nodeId`; scenario 9 explicitly opens a graph with a different declaration `nodeId` alongside. These explicit modes keep the fixture runnable while dispatch authority moves to declaration identity.\n\n## Typed workspace-edge checks\n10–11. Open **Authored Typed Edge Source** and **Target**, then use **Connect graphs** as instructed. Zoom out: expect a thick magenta dashed `smoke-signal` edge with EX/IM projections. Attempting class `default` must be rejected.\n12–13. Open **Typed Export Bridge** and **Typed Import Bridge** together. Zoom out: expect the Bridge-resolved route to use the same `smoke-signal` rendering vocabulary.\n\n## Workspace capture\n14. Open **Workspace Capture Smoke Suite** and follow its checklist. Arrange four graphs, select three, create a typed workspace edge within that selection, save the selection as an ordinary graph, reopen it, and expand its Portal-backed projections."
        }
      }
